    "doi": "https://doi.org/10.1038/nclimate2870",
    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Negative emissions technologies",
    "problem": "Climate stabilization scenarios increasingly rely on large-scale negative emissions technologies, yet the feasibility of this deployment is uncertain due to poorly understood biophysical limits, resource requirements (land, water, energy), and economic costs, which challenge their widespread application.",
    "method": "This paper presents a bottom-up analysis that quantifies and compares the biophysical impacts\u2014on land, water, energy, and nutrients\u2014and economic costs of different negative emissions technologies to determine their global resource limits and feasibility for achieving climate goals.",
    "task": "The task is to quantify the potential global impacts of different negative emissions technologies on land, water, energy, and nutrients to determine the biophysical and economic limits to their widespread application in achieving climate goals.",
